  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Place water, rice, and spices in a 6-quart electric pressure cooker, then stir to combine. Lock lid and set to pressure cook on HIGH for 3 minutes. Allow the pressure to release naturally for 10 minutes, then carefully release any remaining pressure and remove the lid. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 ½ cups water\n1 cup arborio rice\n½ tsp cinnamon, ground\n¼ tsp salt\n⅛ tsp nutmeg, ground"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the rice is done, place cream, eggs, and vanilla in a small bowl, then whisk to combine the custard mixture.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ cup heavy whipping cream\n1 tsp vanilla extract"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Set the pressure cooker to sauté on HIGH. Add additional cream and sugar to the rice, then stir to combine. Stirring constantly, slowly add the custard mixture to the rice in a steady stream. Continue to cook, stirring constantly, until the rice pudding is thickened, 3-4 minutes. Add raisins, stir once more to combine, and remove from heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "heavy whipping cream\n¾ cup granulated sugar\n½ cup raisins"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Enjoy warm, sprinkled with additional cinnamon (if desired), or chill completely and refrigerate if you prefer your rice pudding cool.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "¼ tsp cinnamon, ground"
    }
  ],
